  "topIssues": [
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOL-xLQ87mfbGO",
      "title": "CCI Stats Cronjob Failures",
      "author": "hdcesario-op",
      "number": 542,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "body": "<!--\nNeed help?\nRefer to our contributing guidelines for additional information about making a good issue:\nhttps://github.com/ethereum-optimism/.github/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\n-->\n\n**Bug Description**\n\nThe `cci-stats` service fails when processing pipelines that contain jobs without test metadata. When the CircleCI API returns a `not found` error for test metadata (common for setup/deploy jobs or jobs without tests), the error propagates and causes the entire pipeline processing to fail, preventing ingestion of other pipelines and generating alert noise/fatigue in our on-call shifts\n\n\n**Steps to Reproduce**\n\n1. Run the cci-stats service with valid configuration (CCI_KEY, DATABASE_URI, PROJECT_SLUG, etc.)\n\n1. The service processes pipelines and attempts to fetch test metadata for all jobs\n\n1. When it encounters a job without test metadata, the [CircleCI API](https://circleci.com/docs/api/v2/#tag/Job/operation/getTests) returns \"not found\"\n\n1. The error is not handled gracefully and bubbles up, causing the K8s job to fail\n\n**Expected behavior**\nJobs without test metadata should be handled gracefully:\n* When the CircleCI API returns `not found` for test metadata, the service should log a debug message and return an empty test metadata slice\n* The pipeline processing should continue for other jobs\n* Only actual errors (network failures, authentication issues, etc.) should cause pipeline processing to fail\n* The service should be resilient to jobs that legitimately don't have test metadata available\n\n**Environment Information:**\n - Operating System: `golang:1.23.4-alpine3.20`\n - Package Version (or commit hash): `cci-stats:v0.0.2@sha256:647a100543efaf3197b71a7a1723a9ef3ff225f80ec897caa9e5f03a85afdf9f`\n**Configurations:**\nCommand line flags or environment variables you're using.\n\n**Logs:**\n```\nerror: failed to ingest pipelines: failed to process pipeline: failed to fetch test metadata: failed to fetch test metadata: failed to list test metadata: not found\n```\n\n**Additional context**\n[Slack](https://oplabs-pbc.slack.com/archives/C042355092L/p1769606646201419)\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-28T19:22:59Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-01-29T14:32:47Z",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "commentCount": 2
    }
  ],
  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ86-TEgK",
      "title": "feat(proxyd): tx validation middleware",
      "author": "charlesma4",
      "number": 539,
      "body": "<!-- Contributions welcome! See https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/.github/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md -->\r\n\r\n**Description**\r\n\r\nTransaction validation middleware, which allows you to specify a custom URL and interface (if needed) to pass transactions to for additional checks. Either allows the transaction through, or blocks it.\r\n\r\nMiddleware endpoint can have a custom request interface, but response interface must conform to a single field `{block: bool}`, and can include optional errorCode/Msg fields.\r\n\r\nFails open in case the middleware returns an error code.\r\n\r\nSupports `eth_sendRawTransaction | eth_sendBundle` currently.\r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\nFull unit testing for tx validation middleware file, including all utility functions.\r\n\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-20T20:24:35Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-01-29T06:10:34Z",
      "additions": 835,
      "deletions": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ86_8bJT",
      "title": "fix(service): handle missing test metadata error",
      "author": "hdcesario-op",
      "number": 543,
      "body": "**Description**\r\n\r\nFixes a bug where the cci-stats service fails when processing pipelines containing jobs without test metadata. The CircleCI API returns a \"not found\" error for jobs that don't have test metadata (e.g., setup/deploy jobs, jobs without tests), which previously caused the entire pipeline ingestion to fail.\r\nThis PR adds graceful error handling in fetchTestMetadata to detect \"not found\" errors from the CircleCI API, log them at debug level, and return an empty test metadata slice instead of propagating the error. This allows pipeline processing to continue for other jobs.\r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\nNo tests were added. This codebase currently has no test infrastructure (0 existing tests). The fix is minimal and focused on error handling for an external API response. The change is straightforward: checking error messages and returning an empty slice, which is safe and follows Go idioms.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\nProduction Error log:\r\n\r\n```\r\nerror: failed to ingest pipelines: failed to process pipeline: failed to fetch test metadata: failed to fetch test metadata: failed to list test metadata: not found\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Metadata**\r\n\r\n- Fixes #542 \r\nContext: [Slack](https://oplabs-pbc.slack.com/archives/C042355092L/p1769606646201419)\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-28T19:53:03Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-01-29T12:02:17Z",
      "additions": 75,
      "deletions": 0
    },
